        {
          "id": 1906050,
          "username": "Mansi_2_1",
          "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/m/8491ac/{size}.png",
          "created_at": "2026-10-05T11:19:41.901Z",
          "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group quote-modified\" data-username=\"Techspawn2\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"608148\" data-full=\"true\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/t/b5ac83/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Techspawn2:</div>\n<blockquote></blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Hello,</p>\n<p>We had a very similar issue, especially during promotions when orders could come in from different channels at almost the same time. Scheduled inventory syncs were fine normally, but during busy periods they could definitely lead to overselling.</p>\n<p>We ended up using <strong>Commercium by ConstaCloud</strong>, and it helped us move away from relying purely on fixed-interval syncing. It connects Shopify with marketplaces and keeps inventory and orders synchronized across the channels, with a single place to manage the different sales channels.</p>\n<p>If the main issue you’re having is the delay between a sale and the inventory update on your other channels, it might be worth checking out. I’d still recommend discussing your specific flash-sale scenario with their team to make sure the marketplaces you’re using support the real-time/event-based flows you need.</p>\n<p>You can have a look here: <a href=\"https://constacloud.com/commercium/index.html\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Commerce Orchestration System | Commercium by ConstaCloud</a></p>",
