        {
          "id": 1913521,
          "username": "Jules_StockPont",
          "avatar_template": "https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/j/c68b51/{size}.png",
          "created_at": "2026-10-13T20:33:17.916Z",
          "cooked": "<p>For Etsy specifically, an inventory update is a full listing-inventory write (all variations at once), not a single quantity change, so “real-time” is bounded by how the app batches writes and by Etsy’s rate limits. During a drop, a threshold rule (publish 0 below N units on the secondary channel) is the safest net.</p>\n<p>Disclosure: I’m the founder of StockPont, a Shopify↔Etsy sync for EU sellers, pre-launch: <a href=\"https://stockpont.com/en\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">Etsy &amp; Shopify guides for sellers | StockPont</a></p>",
