    "ai_summary": {
      "id": 1565786,
      "summarized_text": "Sellers are seeking reliable Shopify-to-marketplace inventory synchronization during flash sales, when near-simultaneous orders can cause overselling before scheduled updates run. The original poster wants event-triggered updates, protection against concurrent orders, and ideally a shared order dashboard; the specific marketplaces involved remain unspecified.\n\nReplies caution that “real-time” syncing cannot guarantee immediate availability on marketplace storefronts: retailer systems may take 30–60 minutes to reflect updates, and Shopify API limits can create backlogs. Etsy also requires inventory writes for all listing variations and imposes rate limits. Suggested safeguards include publishing zero inventory once stock falls below a set threshold, accepting that this may leave some units unsold, and reserving stock by channel to prevent race conditions.\n\nOne commenter recommended Commercium, while advising the seller to confirm support for their exact marketplaces and event-based flows. Another mentioned a pre-launch Shopify–Etsy sync tool and disclosed being its founder. No solution was verified as fully resolving the problem; the discussion remains open, with platform limits and the seller’s channel mix still important unanswered factors.",
